{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L38","fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"]},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>"},{"type":"text","text":"; a grid is numbered row-major."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":", once per edge, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"text":" once each, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"text":" once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"text":" breaks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"text":". Each target is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yields them by count, rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"lazy.filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a fixed neighbor list: the filter calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its predicate per element and keeps the unfiltered iterator’s state, and in the benchmarks on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1000 × 1000 grid it cost 1.2–1.8× the precomputed row (breadth-first layers, components,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Positions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" An edge’s position is "},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", unique even among parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so "},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight closure reading "},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":": a closure has no identity and is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/directedgraph-implementations","title":"DirectedGraph Implementations"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs","title":"ImplicitGraphs","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/init(vertexCount:successors:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(1): calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": 